get_worker_trace:
Inspect an intent's (work's) execution trace (unlike get_worker_output, which returns only the final conclusion). Three modes:
① intent_id only → returns a summary stream for every step (summary≤100 characters, includes step_id; action outlines only, without full output);
② intent_id + q → returns only step summaries matching the keyword (searches summaries and full output; still returns only summary; use ③ for full content);
③ intent_id + step_ids → returns full content (detail) for those steps; at most 5 per call. If more are requested, only the first 5 are returned, with omissions reported in notice/omitted_step_ids.
Typical workflow: use ①/② to locate suspicious step_ids, then ③ to fetch full output. Excludes thinking steps. Supports historical traces from directly related tasks; their results include source_task_id/inherited=true and are read-only.
